        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: उफनना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उफनना — uphannā — \"to swell up; to boil over\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भारी बारिश के बाद नदी उफन गई। bhārī bāriś ke bād nadī uphan gaī. After the heavy rain the river swelled over its banks."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): वह नदी उफनी, vah nadī uphnī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उफनना (uphannā) is inherited from utphaṇati, a form CDIAL reconstructs (CDIAL 1836). Milk on the fire उफनता है, and so does a river in flood."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
